  "title": "Self-driving RC car (Donkey Car)",
  "summary": "RC car template: a self-driving RC car, Donkey Car, autonomous car, robot car, rover, 1/16 scale RC car with a Raspberry Pi and a camera; or a small Arduino 2WD robot car with no camera. Rows: RC car chassis (with its own drive motor, ESC, steering servo and battery), Raspberry Pi computer, microSD card, wide-angle camera, PCA9685 servo driver, USB power bank, jumper wires, printed roll cage and top plate, screws, optional LiPo pack and charger. Detection labels: rc car chassis, wheel, raspberry pi board, camera module, servo driver board, power bank, jumper wires. Starting point, not a verified design; the docs do not state the chassis battery voltage.",
  "references": [
    {
      "url": "https://docs.donkeycar.com/guide/build_hardware/",
      "title": "Donkey Car docs: build the hardware",
      "licence": "MIT (code); docs licence [unverified]",
      "used_for": "parts list, PCA9685 wiring note, USB battery; cited and quoted briefly, no text copied"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://docs.donkeycar.com/cars/supported_cars/",
      "title": "Donkey Car docs: supported cars",
      "licence": "MIT (code); docs licence [unverified]",
      "used_for": "chassis choice (Magnet or an alternative, 1/16 scale); battery voltage, ESC and servo specs are not stated there"
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
